From a6c74b357742be6e3a698e6138e174c7998c11af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:51:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Native: let callers choose the DXGI adapter, add batched
 pixel readback and render-target diagnostics

Bumps the player API from 14 to 15 and adds FFF.Native capabilities. Because
FFF3FP_Create rejects a mismatched version and requires sizeof(configuration)
to cover every field, the kernel and its host MUST ship in lockstep -- the
companion FFF.Player change is in the following commit.

- FFF3FPConfiguration gains preferredAdapterIndex (appended at the end, so the
  struct grows 72 -> 80 bytes). -1 keeps the existing policy (pick the adapter
  that drives the monitor containing the output window); 0..15 select an
  adapter by its IDXGIFactory1::EnumAdapters1 index. Out-of-range or failed
  enumeration falls back to the built-in policy rather than failing hard.
  The field defaults to -1 in the header so a host that merely zero-initialises
  the struct cannot accidentally pin playback to adapter #0.
- EnsureDevice() honours the preference before the monitor match, and reports
  the adapter actually backing the device through OutputDebugStringA. The
  diagnostic formats into a fixed-size stack buffer because EnsureDevice() is
  noexcept and must not be able to terminate on allocation failure.
- FFF3FP_ReadVideoPixelRegion reads a rectangular region in one staging copy
  plus one Map, instead of one GPU round trip per pixel. The destination size
  is compared in 64-bit (width * height * 4 wraps in uint32), and a region that
  does not fit inside the swapchain is rejected with InvalidArgument instead of
  being silently truncated to a compact row pitch.
- FFF3FP_GetRenderTargetInfo reports swapchain/client/destination sizes. It
  returns InvalidState while no swapchain exists, so a caller can never mistake
  an all-zero struct for a real 0x0 target when mapping pixel-probe
  coordinates.
- SetViewTransform writes the atomic view state directly instead of queueing a
  playback command, which removes a pan latency on HD/HDR sources. Its disc
  guard now reads an atomic flag rather than the worker-owned unique_ptr, since
  this entry point runs on the caller's thread.
- Adds a version resource so the DLL reports the API version it was built
  against.
- .gitignore gains a vcpkg_installed/ rule that matches at any depth; the
  existing third_party/ entry does not cover other locations.
